$DATUM Aldehyde 35: To a stirred solution of alcohol 34 (158 mg, 0.244 mmol)
were added iodobenzen diacetate (102 mg, 0.317 mmol) and TEMPO (11.4 mg,
0.073 mmol) at room temperature. The mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 1 h, diluted with saturated aqueous Na2S2O3, and
extracted with EtOAc (3 × 5 mL). The combined extracts were washed with
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 (5 mL) and brine (5 mL), dried (Na2SO4),
filtered, and concentrated. The residual oil was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (14 g, hexane-EtOAc 10:1 to 5:1). Yield:
(157 mg, quant.), colorless oil. [α]D25 +9.8° (c 1.03, CHCl3); IR (neat,
cm-1) 2948, 2931, 2851, 2720, 1726, 1616, 1517, 1428, 1342, 1249, 1104,
1035, 825, 754, 703, 616; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.69 (dd, J= 2.2, 2.0
Hz, 1H), 7.68-7.65 (m, 4H), 7.44-7.23 (m, 8H), 6.88 (d, J= 8.5 Hz, 2H),
5.38 (s, 1H), 5.23 (d, J= 9.4 Hz, 1H), 4.06 (m, 1H), 3.90 (m, 1H), 3.83
(s, 3H), 3.83-3.69 (m, 2H), 3.72 (t, J= 7.2 Hz, 1H), 3.16 (s, 3H), 3.07
(m, 1H), 2.42 (ddd, J= 16.2, 6.1, 2.0 Hz, 1H), 2.34 (ddd, J= 16.2, 8.1,
2.2 Hz, 1H), 1.99 (m, 1H), 1.92-1.77 (m, 2H), 1.61 (s, 3H), 1.60 (m, 1H),
1.58 (dt, J= 12.1, 2.5 Hz, 1H), 1.44 (dt, J= 12.1, 11.0 Hz, 1H), 1.08 (d,
J= 6.7 Hz, 3H), 1.06 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 201.7, 159.8,
135.7, 134.0, 134.0, 133.8, 133.6, 131.8, 129.7, 129.7, 127.8, 127.4,
113.6, 100.3, 83.3, 73.7, 73.6, 59.9, 55.7, 55.4, 51.2, 39.5, 38.9, 37.2,
27.5, 27.0, 21.3, 19.4 10.7; HRMS (ESI) m/z 667.3439, calcd for
C39H52O6SiNa [M+Na]+ 667.3431.
