$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1.4 Catalytic oxidation of alcohol 0.25 mmol α-phenylethanol was
dissolved in 1 mL solvent followed by the addition of 0.35 mmol oxygen
source PhI(OAc)2 and 2 mol% catalyst. The mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 1 h. After the reaction was complete, column
chromatography was used to remove the catalyst (eluent : ethyl acetate).
HP 6890GC/MS5973 gas chromatograph mass spectrometer was applied for
qualitative analysis, and HP 6890 gas chromatograph (OV-17 capillary
column) for quantitative analysis. acetophenone, 97 %
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Highly efficient oxidation of secondary alcohol catalyzed by
Mn(II)-saloph at ambient temperature
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
