$DATUM Aldehyde 18. To a solution of alcohol 17 (477 mg, 1.00 mmol, 1.0 equiv)
in CH2Cl2 (30 mL) was added iodobenzene diacetate (BAIB) (966 mg, 3.00
mmol, 3.0 equiv) and TEMPO (45.6 mg, 0.30 mmol, 0.3 equiv) at 0°C. After
0.5 h at this temperature, a saturated aqueous Na2S2O3 solution was added
and the bilayer system was allowed to stir at 0°C for an additional 0.5
h. The organic phase was then separated, the aqueous layer extracted with
CH2Cl2 (2 x 10 mL), and the combined organic extracts were washed with
brine, dried (MgSO4) and filtered. After concentration under reduced
pressure, the crude aldehyde was purified by flash column chromatography
(silica gel, 5% AcOEt in hexanes) to obtain aldehyde 18 (465 mg, 98%) as
a colorless oil Aldehyde 18, yield 465 mg, 98% Rf = 0.63 (silica gel, 20%
EtOAc in hexanes); [α]D25 = +45.3 (c = 0.7, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 0.00, 0.01, 0.03 and 0.04 (4 s, 12 H), 0.80 (s, 9 H), 0.84
(s, 9 H), 0.94 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3 H), 1.10 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3 H), 1.26 and
1.31 (2 s, 6 H), 1.91 (ddc, J = 7.0, 3.3 Hz, 1 H), 2.60 (ddc, J = 7.0,
2.1 Hz, 1 H), 3.65 (dd, J = 7.3 Hz, 1 H), 3.70 (dd, J = 6.5, 3.3 Hz, 1
H), 3.96 (c, J = 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 3.97-4.02 (m, 2 H), 9.75 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1
H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = -4.9, -4.2, -3.9, -3.8, 11.2, 11.6,
17.8, 18.3, 25.3, 25.6, 26.1, 26.3, 44.3, 50.6, 68.0, 73.3, 75.26, 75.3,
108.8, 204.9.
