$DATUM (2R)-1-tert-Butyl 2-formyl-5-oxopyrrolidine-1,2-dicarboxylate methyl
ester (3) To a solution of 6A (6.4 g, 23.4 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (60 ml) was
added TEMPO (365 mg, 2.34 mmol) and PhI(OAc)2 (8.30 g, 25.8 mmol) at room
temperature. The reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature under
argon for 26 h, filtered through thin silica gel pad, eluted with ethyl
acetate, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (elution with hexane/EtOAc = 8:1
then 2:1) to give 3 (6.2 g, 98%) as colorless oil: (2R)-1-tert-Butyl
2-formyl-5-oxopyrrolidine-1,2-dicarboxylate methyl ester (3), yield 6.2
g, 98% [α]29D +27.5 (c 0.95, CHCl3); FTIR (neat) 3541, 1798, 1763, 1740,
1717, 1458, 1437, 1371, 1321, 1293, 1257, 1154 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 9.98 (s, 1H), 3.86 (s, 3H), 2.53-2.61 (m, 2H), 2.20-2.24 (m,
2H), 1.45 (s, 9H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 193.6, 172.0, 169.7, 148.7,
84.8, 72.1, 53.2, 30.3, 27.7, 24.9; HRMS (FAB) m/z (M+H)+ calcd for
[C12H17NO6+H]+ 272.1134, found 272.1142.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
