$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Aldehyde carbonate (-)-73: To a stirred solution of hydroxy carbonate
(-)-24-2 (0.57 g, 0.57 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) at 25°C was added
PhI(OAc)2 (5.0 equiv, 1.0 g, 2.85 mmol) and TEMPO (1.0 equiv, 0.10 mg,
0.57 mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred for 24 h and then quenched
with saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (10 mL). The resulting mixture was
extracted with Et2O (2 × 20 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated in
vacuo. The crude residue was purified by flash column chromatography
(silica, Et2O/hexanes, 10 → 40%) to furnish aldehyde carbonate (-)-73
(175 mg, 0.178 mmol, 98%) as a colorless oil. compound (-)-73, yield (175
mg, 0.178 mmol, 98%) Rf = 0.50 (silica, EtOAc:hexanes, 1:6); [α]25 D =
-28.6 (c = 1.6, CHCl3); IR (film): νmax = 2953s, 2870s, 1750s, 1719m,
1441m, 1266m, 1090s cm-1; 1H NMR (C6D6, 600 MHz): δ = 9.82 (s, 1 H), 7.40
(d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2 H), 7.22 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.18 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 2
H), 7.11 (m, 2 H), 6.02 (s, 1 H), 5.77 (s, 1 H), 4.89 (s, 1 H), 4.85 (s,
1 H), 4.77 (s, 2 H), 4.71 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.66 (s, J = 7.2 Hz, 1
H), 4.64 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.62 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.56 - 4.41
(m, 5 H), 4.35 (s, 1 H), 4.20 (s, 1 H), 3.92 (d, J = 11.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.89
(d, J = 11.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.71 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 2 H), 3.36 (s, 3 H), 2.94 (t,
J = 8.4 Hz, 1 H), 2.70 (m, 2 H), 2.63 (s, 1 H), 2.51 (m, 1 H), 2.31 (m, 3
H), 2.16 - 1.98 (m, 12 H), 1.79 (t, J = 6.6 Hz, 1 H), 1.72 (s, 3 H), 1.36
(s, 3 H), 1.28 (s, 3 H), 1.25 (s, 3 H), 1.17 (s, 3 H), 0.97 (t, J = 7.8
Hz, 2 H), 0.01 (s, 9 H) ppm; 13C NMR (C6D6, 125 MHz): δ = 199.15, 155.39,
148.07, 144.36, 139.01, 138.57, 128.74, 125.41, 111.79, 99.31, 95.89,
94.99, 89.99, 89.27, 83.15, 78.18, 77.57, 77.34, 75.86, 70.66, 69.97,
67.54, 66.19, 64.90, 63.72, 54.71, 54.70, 52.45, 51.44, 50.99, 49.50,
46.21, 37.06, 31.75, 29.56, 27.46, 25.87, 25.81, 25.68, 25.16, 24.39,
24.08, 23.68, 22.29, 20.37, 18.38, -1.24 ppm; HRMS calcd for
C57H82O12SiNa+ [M + Na+] 1009.5467 found 1009.5439.
