$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (2S,4R)-5-{[(1,1-Dimethylethyl)(dimethyl)silyl]oxy}-2,4-dimethylpentanal
(8): To a stirred solution of alcohol 7 (2.46 g, 10.0 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (35
mL) a mixture of iodobenzene diacetate (4.83g, 15 mmol, 1.5 equiv) and
TEMPO (78 mg, 0.5 mmol, 0.05 equiv) was added in five portions over a
period of 30 min. The orange reaction mixture was stirred for an
additional 60 min at 23 °C before a 25% solution of sodium thiosulphate
(10 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred for 15 min and the organic
phase was separated. The aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (15 mL),
and the combined organic layers were washed with saturated aqueous NaHCO3
solution (2 × 30 mL), and brine. The organic phase was dried over Na2SO4,
and filtered through a short pad of silica gel (2 cm), followed by
washing the pad with CH2Cl2 (2 × 10 mL). After removal of the solvent in
vacuo, the residue was subjected to a high-vacuum (0.03 mm Hg)
distillation at room temperature with the receiver flask immersed in
liquid nitrogen, in order to remove PhI. The oily aldehyde (2.4 g, 98%)
was immediately used for the next step.
(2S,4R)-5-{[(1,1-Dimethylethyl)(dimethyl)silyl]oxy}-2,4-dimethylpentanal
(8) , yield 2.4 g, 98% Rf = 0.64 (EtOAc/petroleum ether, 1:9); 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.02 (s, 6H, (CH3)2Si), 0.88 (m, 1H,), (s, 9H,
(CH3)3CSi), 0.87-0.90 (m, CHCHHCH, (CH3)CHCH2O), 1.08 (d, 3H, J = 6.8 Hz,
(CH3)CHCHO), 1.60-1.72 (m, 1H, CHCHHCH), 1.80-1.90 (m, 1H, CHCH2O),
2.40-2.51 (m, 1H, CHCHO), 3.41 (d, 2H, J = 5.6 Hz, CH2OSi), 9.56 (d, 1H,
J = 2.3 Hz, CHO); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =-5.5 ((CH3)2Si), 14.3
((CH3)CHCHO), 17.1((CH3)CHCH2OSi), 18.3 ((CH3)3CSi), 25.9 ((CH3)3CSi),
33.4 (CHCH2O), 34.6 (CHCH2CH), 44.2 (CHCHO), 67.8 (CH2OSi), 205.4 (CHO).
