$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Aldehyde carbonate (+)-51: To a stirred solution of hydroxy carbonate
(+)-49-1 (410 mg, 0.414 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) at 25 °C were added
PhI(OAc)2 (3.0 equiv, 0.34 g, 1.20 mmol) and AZADO (0.1 equiv, 7 mg,
0.041 mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred for 24 h and then quenched
with a mixture of saturated aqueous solutions of NaHCO3 (5 mL) and
Na2S2O3 (5 mL). The resulting mixture was extracted with Et2O (2 x 15
mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 5 - 15%)
to furnish aldehyde carbonate (+)-51 as a foam, yield 400 mg, 0.405 mmol,
97%. Rf = 0.40 (silica, Et2O:hexanes, 3:7); [α]25D = +15.6 (c = 1.5,
CHCl3); IR (film): νmax = 2951s, 1751s, 1441w, 1373m, 1266m, 1195m, 1039s
cm-1; 1H NMR (C6D6, 600 MHz): δ = 10.29 (s, 1 H), 7.40 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2
H), 7.31 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2 H), 7.20 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2 H), 7.15 (m, 2 H),
7.09 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.07 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.26 (s, 1 H), 5.88
(s, 1 H), 4.93 (s, 1 H), 4.87 (s, 1 H), 4.71 - 4.64 (m, 7 H), 4.60 - 4.57
(m, 3 H), 4.51 (s, 2 H), 4.50 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1 H), 4.36 (d, J = 11.4
Hz, 1 H), 4.34 (d, J = 11.4 Hz, 1 H), 4.11 (s, 1 H), 3.69 (m, 1 H), 3.46
(s, 3 H), 3.35 (m, 1 H), 3.00 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.75 (t, J = 12.0 Hz,
1 H), 2.62 (d, J = 3.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.49 (m, 3 H), 2.22 - 1.95 (m, 9 H),
1.87 (m, 4 H), 1.80 (m, 1 H), 1.64 (s, 3 H), 1.64 (m, 2 H), 1.41 (s, 9
H), 1.40 (m, 1 H), 1.23 (s, 3 H), 0.99 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 2 H), 0.00 (s, 9
H) ppm; 13C NMR (C6D6, 150 MHz): δ = 202.51, 155.86, 144.52, 144.09,
139.02, 138.66, 133.78, 133.65, 133.11, 111.65, 98.11, 96.90, 95.11,
94.90, 91.07, 82.99, 77.71, 74.10, 71.30, 70.02, 69.88, 69.48, 67.38,
66.37, 63.40, 56.26, 54.75, 54.27, 51.86, 48.65, 45.95, 45.92, 42.59,
32.21, 31.01, 30.47, 29.60, 28.35, 26.18, 25.94, 25.03, 24.22, 23.73,
19.90, 17.96, -1.35 ppm; HRMS calcd for C57H82O12SiNa+ [M + Na+]
1009.5567 found 1009.5474.
