$DATUM Aldeyde (-)-99: To a stirred solution of hydroxy carbonate (-)-97 (560
mg, 0.463 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) at 25 °C were added PhI(OAc)2 (2.0
equiv, 0.30 g, 0.926 mmol) and AZADO (0.1 equiv, 7 mg, 0.046 mmol). The
resulting mixture was stirred for 24 h and then quenched with saturated
aqueous NaHCO3 solution (10 mL). The resulting mixture was extracted with
Et2O (2 x 20 mL), dried (MgSO4), and concentrated under reduced pressure.
The crude residue was purified by flash column chromatography (silica,
EtOAc/hexanes, 5 - 20%) to furnish aldehyde carbonate (-)-99 as a white
foam, yield 540 mg, 0.447 mmol, 96%. Rf = 0.40 (silica, Et2O:hexanes,
4:6); [α]25D = -77.50 (c = 0.2, CHCl3); IR (film): νmax = 2952s, 2891s,
1750s, 1714m, 1441w, 1377m, 1265s, 1039s cm-1; 1H NMR (C6D6, 500 MHz): δ
= 9.91 (s, 1 H), 7.51 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 2 H), 7.33 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 2 H),
7.22 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 2 H), 7.19 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2 H), 7.10 - 7.07 (m, 2
H), 6.05 (s, 1 H), 5.71 (s, 1 H), 5.25 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.94 (d, J =
6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.93 (s, 1 H), 4.79 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.78 (d, J = 12.5
Hz, 1 H), 4.77 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.70 - 4.67 (m, 3 H), 4.64 (d, J =
12.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.56 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.53 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.47
(d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.43 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.37 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1
H), 4.35 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.34 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.24 (t, J =
