$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Allylic Alcohol. To a solution of alcohol (15.5 g, 0.03 mol) in CH2Cl2
(50 mL) at room temperature was added bisacetoxyiodobenzene (9.61 g, 0.03
mol). After addition of TEMPO (437 mg, 3.0 mmol), the clear orange
solution was stirred at room temperature for 2 h. The reaction was then
diluted with CH2Cl2 (150 mL) and treated with saturated sodium sulfite
solution until it became colorless. Upon separation of the layers, the
aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 200 mL). The combined
organic layers were dried over Na2SO4, concentrated, and purified by
column chromatography (2% EtOAc in hexanes). aldehyde as a colorless oil,
14.8 g, 96%. [α]D20 -21.6 (c 1.95, CHCl3). 1H NMR(500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 9.67
(t, J = 2.22 Hz, 1 H), 4.20-4.17 (m, 1 H), 3.62-3.59 (m, 1 H), 2.65 (ddd,
J = 1.8, 4.0, 15.9 Hz, 1 H), 2.43 (ddd, J = 2.9, 8.2, 15.7 Hz, 1 H),
1.66-1.60 (m, 1 H), 1.47-1.31 (m, 1 H), 1.30-1.12 (m, 30 H), 0.92-0.88
(m, 18 H), 0.86 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3 H), 0.62-0.48 (m, 12 H). 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3): δ 201.9, 75.1, 70.8, 46.1, 32.1, 30.6, 30.0, 29.9, 29.8,
29.5, 26.7, 22.9, 14.2, 7.0, 5.3, 5.1. IR (thin film): 2930, 2978, 2855,
2716, 1732, 1640, 1414, 1381, 1327, 1240, 1103, 1007, 976, 833, 743, 673
cm-1. HRMS (CI, CH4) calcd for C33H70O3Si2, 569.4785 m/z [M - H]+;
observed, 569.4775 m/z.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of the Proposed Structure of Mucoxin via Regio- and
Stereoselective Tetrahydrofuran Ring-Forming Strategies
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Narayan, Radha S.; Borhan, Babak
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(4), 1416-1429

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME144 STEP1
