$DATUM (Z)-Trimethylsilanyl-4-undecen-1-yn-3-one, 18.
Trimethylsilyl-4-dodecen-1-yn-3-ol (17) (505 mg, 2.00 mmol) and TEMPO (41
mg, 0.26 mmol) were dissolved in CH2Cl2 (2 mL), and, after the addition
of diacetoxy iodosobenzene (838 mg, 2.60 mmol), the reaction mixture was
stirred for 2 h at room temperature. The mixture was then diluted with
CH2Cl2 (4 x 15 mL) and washed with a saturated aqueous sodium thiosulfate
solution (6mL), the aqueous phase was extracted with CH2Cl2 (10 mL), and
the combined organic phases were washed with small portions of a
saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution (5 mL), followed by brine (5mL), and
then dried withMgSO4. Flash chromatography on silica gel with petroleum
ether/ethyl acetate (30/1, v/v) gave
(Z)-trimethylsilanyl-4-dodecen-1-yn-3-on (18) as a colorless oil (475 mg,
95% yield). Compound 18: E/Z ratio 1:5 (determined by chiral GC, system
B) (29). MS(EI):m/z (%)=251 (M ++1, 24), 235 (26), 221 (19), 205 (44),
153 (57), 139 (100), 125 (90), 97 (43), 75 (91). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 6.26 (1H, dt, J=11.6, 7.2Hz), 6.14 (1H, dt, J=11.6, 1.5Hz), 2.70 (2H,
dq, J= 7.2, 1.5 Hz), 1.20-1.48 (10H, m), 0.85 (3H, t, J=7.2 Hz), 0.24
(9H, s).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM E:Z 1:5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure Determination of Bisacetylenic Oxylipins in Carrots (Daucus
carota L.) and Enantioselective Synthesis of Falcarindiol
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Schmiech, Ludger; Alayrac, Carole; Witulski, Bernhard; Hofmann, Thomas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry (2009), 57(22), 11030-11040

