$DATUM Aldehyde carbonate (-)-50: To a stirred solution of hydroxy carbonate
(-)-48-1 (102 mg, 0.103 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL) at 25 °C were added
PhI(OAc)2 (3.0 equiv, 0.1 g, 0.31 mmol) and AZADO (0.1 equiv, 5 mg, 0.01
mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred for 24 h and then quenched with
a mixture of saturated aqueous solutions of NaHCO3 (5 mL) and Na2S2O3 (5
mL). The resulting mixture was extracted with Et2O (2 x 15 mL), dried
(MgSO4), and concentrated in vacuo. The crude residue was purified by
flash column chromatography (silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 9 - 11%) to furnish
aldehyde carbonate (-)-50 as a foam, yield 97 mg, 0.098 mmol, 95%. Rf =
0.32 (silica, EtOAc:hexanes, 1:5); [α]25D = -50.6 (c = 1.0, CHCl3); IR
(film): νmax = 2951s, 1751s, 1441w, 1373m, 1266m, 1195m, 1039s cm-1; 1H
NMR (C6D6, 600 MHz): δ = 9.87 (s, 1 H), 7.48 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2 H), 7.38
(d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2 H), 7.21 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 4 H), 7.12 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1
H), 7.06 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.05 (s, 1 H), 5.75 (s, 1 H), 4.85 (s, 2
H), 4.81 (d, J = 12.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.74 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.68 (d, J =
7.2 Hz, 1 H), 4.65 (d, J = 12.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.61 (d, J = 12.6 Hz, 1 H),
4.55 (s, 1 H), 4.49 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 1 H), 4.44 (d, J = 12.6 Hz, 1 H),
4.41 - 4.38 (m, 3 H), 4.32 (s, 1 H), 4.19 (s, 1 H), 4.09 (d, J = 11.4 Hz,
1 H), 3.90 (d, J = 11.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.64 (m, 1 H), 3.38 (s, 3 H), 3.34 (m,
1 H), 2.95 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1 H), 2.86 (d, J = 3.0 Hz, 1 H), 2.79 (dt, J =
13.8, 3.6 Hz, 1 H), 2.60 - 2.48 (m, 3 H), 2.44 (t, J = 13.8 Hz, 1 H),
2.29 - 2.24 (m, 2 H), 2.20 - 2.08 (m, 4 H), 1.98 (m, 1 H), 1.92 - 1.85
(m, 3 H), 1.80 (m, 1 H), 1.72 (s, 3 H), 1.72 - 1.68 (m, 2 H), 1.59 (m, 1
