$DATUM Aldehyde 40. To a solution of diol 39 (509 mg, 0.83 mmol, 1.00 equiv) in
20 mL of CH2Cl2 were added iodobenzene diacetate (280 mg, 0.87 mmol, 1.05
equiv) and TEMPO (12.9 mg, 82.7 μmol, 0.10 equiv). After 12 h at room
temperature, TLC (1:1 hexanes/EtOAc, UV/anisaldehyde) showed complete
consumption of the starting material and clean formation of the product.
The solvent was removed under reduced pressure, and the residue was
purified by column chromatography (3:1 hexanes/EtOAc → 2:1 hexanes/EtOAc
→ 1:1 hexanes/EtOAc). Aldehyde 40 as a colorless oil (483 mg, 95%). Rf =
0.26; [α]D 20 = -24.5 (c 0.57, CH2Cl2); IR (neat) ν 3430, 2924, 1720,
1655, 1596, 1509, 1454, 1392, 1361, 1275, 1234, 1205, 1189, 1176, 1097,
1019, 976 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 0.88 (1H, m), 0.92 (1H, m),
0.96 (3H, d, J = 6.46 Hz), 1.40 (1H, ddd, J = 3.07 Hz, 12.86 Hz, 16.44
Hz), 1.48 (1H, m), 1.71 (6H, s), 1.75 (1H, m), 1.79 (1H, m), 1.86 (1H,
m), 2.07 (1H, m), 2.46 (3H, s), 2.49 (1H, m), 2.67 (1H, dd, J = 7.45 Hz,
13.95 Hz), 2.72 (1H, dd, J = 5.44 Hz, 13.95 Hz), 3.93 (1H, dd, J = 5.84
Hz, 9.51 Hz), 4.02 (2H, m), 4.94 (1H, m), 5.28 (1H, s), 6.05 (1H, dd, J =
1.27 Hz, 15.68 Hz), 6.54 (1H, dd, J = 4.70 Hz, 15.67 Hz), 6.73 (2H, d, J
= 8.56 Hz), 7.04 (2H, d, J = 8.55 Hz), 7.36 (2H, d, J = 8.13 Hz), 7.79
(2H, d, J = 8.26 Hz), 9.53 (1H, d, J = 2.93 Hz); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 21.8, 22.3, 25.13, 25.14, 25.4, 31.7, 34.0, 34.5, 38.4, 41.5, 51.2,
70.5, 72.7, 78.1, 95.4, 106.7, 115.6, 124.1, 128.1, 129.5, 130.1, 130.6,
132.6, 138.0, 145.3, 156.6, 161.8, 162.0, 203.6; HRMS (ESI+) calcd for
C33H41O9S ([M + H]+) 613.2471, found 613.2444.
