$DATUM A mixture of alcohol xiv (14.4 mg, 0.0370 mmol) and IBX (16.3 mg, 0.0582
mmol) in DMSO was stirred for 1 h at room temperature, and then the
reaction was stopped by adding isopropyl alcohol at 0 °C. After adding
saturated aqueous NaHCO3, the products were extracted with CHCl3 (x3),
and the combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried over
Na2SO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by PTLC
(CHCl3/MeOH = 9/1) to afford enone 19, which was reprecipitated from
hexane/CHCl3 White powders, yield 13.6 mg, 95%. Mp 46.0-46.5 °C.
[α]D24+179 (c 1.3, CHCl3). Rf 0.55 (CHCl3/MeOH=9/1). 1H NMR(δ, CDCl3)
2.13 (s, 3H), 2.22 (dd, 1H, J1 = 14.3, J2 = 5.5 Hz), 2.50-2.74 (m, 2H),
2.58 (dd, 1H, J1 = 14.3, J2 = 2.1 Hz), 3.09 (ddd, 1H, J1 = J2 = 9.4, J3 =
2.9 Hz), 3.19 (ddd, 1H, J1 = J2 = 9.4, J3 = 7.2 Hz), 3.30 (s, 3H), 3.32
(d, 1H, J = 16.2 Hz), 3.65 (ddd, 1H, J1 = 5.5, J2 = 2.1, J3 = 0.7 Hz),
3.70 (dd, 1H, J1 = 16.2, J2 = 5.2 Hz), 3.78 (s, 3H), 3.85 (s, 3H), 5.76
(d, 1H, J = 5.2 Hz), 6.18 (d, 1H, J = 0.7 Hz), 6.74 (s, 1H), 6.81 (s,
1H). 13C NMR(δ, CDCl3) 21.4, 28.9, 40.6, 47.0, 47.1, 55.6, 55.7, 57.9,
61.7, 64.7, 76.2, 111.5, 111.7, 122.8, 123.2, 127.6, 148.2, 148.4, 168.8,
170.7, 194.6. IR (ATR) 2932, 2869, 2829, 1726, 1664, 1610, 1512, 1252,
1226, 1127, 1015, 947, 771 cm-1. Anal. Calcd for C21H25NO6: C, 65.10; H,
6.50; N, 3.62. Found: C, 65.10; H, 6.78; N, 3.43.
