$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Alcohol 14 (1.75 g, 7.12 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (35 mL) and to
this was added. bisacetoxy iodo benzene (4.85 g, 15.06 mmol) followed by
2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-1- piperidinyloxyl TEMPO (110 mg, 0.70 mmol). It was
stirred until TLC shows full consumption of starting material. Sat. Na 2
S 2 O 3(aq) (50 mL) was added, layers were separated, aqueous layer was
further extracted with CH2Cl2, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, concentrated
and purified by column chromatography to give product.
(2S,3R)-2-allyl-3-isopropyl-6-(methoxymethoxy)hexanal (15), (1.66 g, 95%
yield), colorless oil. [α] 20 D = + 39.6 (c 1.1, CHCl3); IR (neat)νmax :
3078, 2928, 1724, 1641, 1438, 1151, 1200, 1112, 1041, 918 cm-1 ; 1 H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ = 9.67 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 1H), 5.81- 5.71 (m, 1H),
5.07-4.99 (m, 2H), 4.59 (s, 2H), 3.47 (t, J = 6.3 Hz, 2H), 3.34 (s, 3H),
2.51- 2.41 (m, 2H), 2.20-2.14 (m, 1H), 1.81-1.73 (m, 1H), 1.70-1.65 (m,
1H), 1.60-1.52 (m, 2H), 1.51-1.40 (m, 1H), 1.36-1.28 (m, 1H), 0.91 (d, J
= 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.90 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H); 13 C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3):
205.1, 136.7, 116.7, 96.6, 68.0, 55.3, 53.6, 44.2, 30.1, 29.9, 29.5,
25.0, 21.2, 20.0. HRMS (ESI): m/z: calcd. for C14H26NaO3 : 265.1756,
found: 265.1758.
