$DATUM Aldehyde 23 (II-YL-166) To a rt solution of alcohol 21 (13.2 g, 28.2
mmol) in dry CH2Cl2 (200 mL) under N2 was added [bis(acetoxy)iodo]benzene
22 (37.2 g, 0.116 mol, 4.1 equiv) in one portion followed by TEMPO (0.72
g, 4.61 mmol, 0.16 equiv), also in one portion. Stirring was continued
for 1.5 h whereafter TLC analysis revealed that all of the starting
alcohol 21 had been consumed and that a single faster-moving major
product had formed. The reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo, Et2O
(50 mL) was added, precipitated solids were filtered off, and the
filtrate was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by SiO2
flash chromatography using petrol:Et2O as eluent (3:1). Aldehyde 23 (12.5
g, 95%) was obtained as a colorless oil. Data for 23: [α]D +9.86 º (c
0.284, CH2Cl2); IR 2936 (s), 2858 (m), 1722 (m), 1429 (w), 1364 (w), 1163
(w), 1107 (s), 1038 (w), 932 (w), 824 (w), 739 (wm), 704 (s), 613 (w)
cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, C6D6, 298K) δ 9.52 (s, 1H, H-6), 7.76-7.64 (m, 4H,
Ph), 7.30-7.16 (m, 6H, Ph), 4.14 (dd, 1H, J = 6.5, 13.1 Hz, H-8), 3.99
(dd, 1H, J = 6.4, 8.2 Hz, H-9a), 3.69 (m, 1H, H-12a), 3.60 (m, 1H,
H-12b), 3.52 (dd, 1H, J = 6.9, 7.9 Hz, H-9b), 2.32 (m, 1H, H-7), 1.91 (m,
1H, H-11a), 1.77 (m, 1H, H-11b), 1.65-1.42 (m, 8 H, cyclohex), 1.30-1.15
(m, 2H, cyclohex), 1.12 (s, 9H, t -Bu) ppm; 13C NMR (125 MHz, C6D6, 298K)
δ 201.74 (C-6), 135.90 (Ph), 133.76 (Ph q), 133.70 (Ph q), 130.05 (Ph),
130.03 (Ph), 109.27 (-O-C-O-), 74.17 (C-8), 67.98 (C-9), 62.00 (C-12),
53.20 (C-7), 36.65 (cyclohex), 35.07 (cyclohex), 29.12 (C-11), 26.97
(-C(Me)3), 25.49 (cyclohex), 24.28 (cyclohex), 24.10 (cyclohex), 19.26
(-C(Me)3) ppm; VG 70-SE Positive Ion FAB HRMS: Calcd. for C28H38NaO4Si
(M+Na)+: 489.24369. Found: 489.24277.
