$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (Z)-2-Decenal, 16. Diacetoxyiodosobenzene (DIB; 2.83 g, 8.79 mmol) was
added to a solution of (Z)-2-decenol (15) (1.25 g, 8.01 mmol) and
2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-piperidinyloxyl (TEMPO) (138 mg, 0.88 mmol) in CH2Cl2
(8 mL) and stirred for 2 h at room temperature. Thereafter, the reaction
mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 (30 mL) and washed with a saturated,
aqueous sodium thiosulfate solution (25 mL). The product was extracted
with CH2Cl2 (10 mL) and the combined organic phases were washed with a
saturated NaHCO3 solution (15 mL), followed by brine (15mL), and was then
dried withMgSO4. The crude product was purified by flash chromatography
on silica gel using petroleum ether/ethyl acetate (8/1, v/v) to give
(Z)-2-decenal (16) as a colorless oil (1.17 g, 7.61 mmol, 95% yield).
Compound 16: E/Z ratio 1:32 (determined by chiral GC, system A) (29). MS
(EI): m/z (%)=155 (M++1, 100), 154 (31), 153 (19), 137 (44), 95 (20), 81
(28). 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3): 10.08 (1H, d, J= 8.2Hz), 6.64 (1H, dt,
J=11.1, 8.2Hz), 5.96 (1H, ddt, J=11.1, 8.2, 1.5Hz), 2.60 (2H, q, J=7.2
Hz), 1.24-1.55 (10H, m), 0.89 (3H, t, J=7.0 Hz). 13C NMR(100MHz,CDCl3): δ
190.9, 153.5, 130.1, 58.5, 31.8 (t), 29.1 (t), 29.0 (t), 28.9 (t), 27.9
(t), 22.6 (t), 14.0 (q).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM selective oxidation to aldehyde, E:Z 1:32
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Structure Determination of Bisacetylenic Oxylipins in Carrots (Daucus
carota L.) and Enantioselective Synthesis of Falcarindiol
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Schmiech, Ludger; Alayrac, Carole; Witulski, Bernhard; Hofmann, Thomas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Agricultural and Food Chemistry (2009), 57(22), 11030-11040

