$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Aldehyde 18. To a solution of alcohol 17 (477
mg, 1.00 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in CH2Cl2 (30 mL) was added iodobenzene
diacetate (BAIB) (966 mg, 3.00 mmol, 3.0 equiv) and TEMPO (45.6 mg, 0.30
mmol, 0.3 equiv) at 0°C. After 0.5 h at this temperature, a saturated
aqueous Na2S2O3 solution was added and the bilayer system was allowed to
stir at 0°C for an additional 0.5 h. The organic phase was then
separated, the aqueous layer extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 x 10 mL), and the
combined organic extracts were washed with brine, dried (MgSO4) and
filtered. After concentration under reduced pressure, the crude aldehyde
was purified by flash column chromatography (silica gel, 5% AcOEt in
hexanes) to obtain aldehyde 18 (465 mg, 98%) as a colorless oil Aldehyde
82. The oxidation of alcohol 81 (140 mg, 0.26 mmol) was carried out
exactly as described for 18, by treatment with DMP (220 mg, 0.52 mmol,
2.0 equiv), to obtain, after purification by flash column chromatography
(silica gel, 2.5% AcOEt in hexanes), aldehyde 82 (131 mg, 95%) as a
colorless oil Rf = 0.79 (silica gel, 10% EtOAc in hexanes); 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ = -0.01, 0.03, 0.048 and 0.053 (4 s, 12 H), 0.80-0.83 (m,
24 H), 0.92 (d, J = 7.4 Hz, 3 H), 0.98 (d, J =6.8 Hz, 3 H), 1.29 and 1.27
(2 s, 6 H), 1.64-1.56 (m, 1 H), 1.80 (dq, J = 7.1, 2.8 Hz, 1 H), 1.87
(dq, J = 7.3, 2.4 Hz, 1 H), 2.46 (dq, J = 6.9, 2.7 Hz, 1 H), 3.31 (dd, J
= 11.7, 8.5 Hz, 1 H), 3.39 (dd, J = 8.8, 8.7 Hz, 1 H), 3.63 (dd, J =
11.6, 5.1 Hz, 1 H), 3.98 (dd, J = 9.0, 2.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.13 (dd, J = 5.2,
2.8 Hz, 1 H), 9.67 (d, J = 2.7 Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
-4.23, -4.17, -3.8, -3.1, 10.6, 11.3, 11.9, 15.4, 18.1, 18.2, 20.0, 25.8,
25.9, 28.4, 34.8, 40.8, 46.1, 52.9, 65.3, 73.2, 73.3, 76.0, 98.0, 205.1.
