$DATUM (3aR,7S,8aR)-2-Methoxy-7-methylhexahydro-2H-cyclohepta[b]furan-6(7H)-one
(19)3 To a solution of 18 (1.0 g, 4.99 mmol) in CH2Cl2. (9.98 mL) was
added 1-Me-AZADO2 (41.5 mg, 0.25 mmol), PhI(OAc)2 (2.41 g, 7.49 mmol) at
room temperature. After stirring for 30 min at room temperature, the
reaction mixture was quenched with saturated NaHCO3/saturated Na2SO3 (1/1
v/v), and extracted with CH2Cl2. The combined organics were washed with
brine and dried (MgSO4). Concentration and flash chromatography (4:1
hexanes:EtOAc). 19 (921 mg, 93%) as a colorless oil. 19: IR (neat): 1703
cm-1 ; 1H-NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 4.96-4.93 (1H, m), 4.45-4.34 (1H, m),
3.34 (2.4H, s), 3.32 (0.6H, s), 2.74-2.30 (4H, m), 2.14 (0.8H, dd, J =
13.2, 8.4 Hz), 2.04- 1.56 (5.2H, m), 1.11 (2.4H, d, J = 6.8 Hz), 1.10
(0.6H, d, J = 6.8 Hz) ; 13 C-NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 212.6, 212.1, 104.6,
103.3, 81.3, 78.8, 54.7, 54.2, 42.6, 42.3, 42.2, 41.6, 39.9, 39.7, 39.3,
38.9, 35.7, 34.1, 25.5, 25.4, 16.9, 16.8; MS m/z: 198 (M+ ), 84 (100%);
HRMS calcd for C11H18O3 (M+ ): 198.1256, found: 198.1254.
