$DATUM Aldehyde 59. To a solution of alcohol 58 (79 mg, 0.22 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in
CH2Cl2 (5 mL) was added BAIB (212 mg, 0.66 mmol, 3.0 equiv) and TEMPO (10
mg, 0.066 mmol, 0.3 equiv) at 25°C. After 2 h at this temperature, the
reaction mixture was diluted with Et2O and treated with a saturated
aqueous Na2S2O3 solution. The organic phase was then separated, the
aqueous layer extracted with Et2O (2 x 5 mL), and the combined organic
extracts were washed with brine, dried (MgSO4) and filtered. After
concentration under reduced pressure, the crude aldehyde was purified by
flash column chromatography (silica gel, 5% AcOEt in hexanes) to obtain
aldehyde 59 (73 mg, 93%) as a colorless oil: Aldehyde 59, yield 73 mg,
93% Rf = 0.59 (silica gel, 10% EtOAc in hexanes); [α]D25 = -69.2 (c =
0.6, CH2Cl2); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.10 (s, 6 H), 0.72 (d, J =
6.6 Hz, 3 H), 0.93 (s, 9 H), 0.97 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 3 H), 1.13 (d, J = 7.1
Hz, 3 H), 1.32 and 1.42 (2 s, 6 H), 1.85-1.91 (m, 1 H), 1.97 (sext, J =
6.7 Hz, 1 H), 2.55-2.72 (m, 1 H), 3.54 (dd, J = 11.3 Hz, 1 H), 3.69 (dd,
J = 11.5, 5.0 Hz, 1 H), 3.82-3.84 (m, 2 H), 9.77 (d, J = 1.8 Hz, 1 H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = - 4.5, -4.1, 10.2, 12.6, 14.1, 18.1, 18.7,
25.9, 29.5, 30.4, 39.1, 47.8, 66.1, 72.6, 77.0, 98.0, 205.0.
