$DATUM 1-Cyclopropyl-3-phenylpropan-1-one S21 [25] To a solution of alcohol S20
(2.39 g, 13.6 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (14 mL) was added TEMPO (213 mg, 1.36 mmol)
and BAIB (4.81 g, 14.9 mmol) sequentially. The mixture was stirred for 36
h, after which it was diluted with CH2Cl2 (100 mL) and washed with
Na2S2O3 (100 mL). The layers were separated and the aqueous layer
extracted with CH2Cl2 (4 x 70 mL). The combined organic layers were dried
(MgSO4) and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by column chromatography
(SiO2, eluent load, Pentane:EtOAc, 98:2). S21 (2.20 g, 93%) as a
colourless oil. R f = 0.57 (Pentane:EtOAc, 90:10), [UV, Vanillin]. IR
(film) ν max/cm-1 3086, 3063, 3027, 3008, 2928, 1969, 1604, 1584, 1497,
1453, 1387, 1267, 1195, 1100, 1085, 1072, 1032, 1011, 1001, 968. 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ = 7.35-7.28 (2H, m, Ph), 7.26-7.20 (3H, m, Ph),
2.99-2.88 (4H, m, C1H2 and C2H2), 1.98-1.91 (1H, m, CHCO), 1.08-1.02 (2H,
m, 2 x CHAHBCH), 0.92-0.86 (2H, m, 2 x CHAHBCH). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 101 MHz)
δ = 210.0 (C=O), 141.2 (Ar-C), 128.5 (2C, 2 x Ar-CH), 128.4 (2C, 2 x
Ar-CH), 126.1 (Ar-CH), 45.0 (C1H2), 30.0 (C2H2), 20.6 (CHCO), 10.8 (2C, 2
x CH2CH). HRMS (ESI+) Found [M+Na]+ = 197.0938; C12H14ONa requires
197.0937, Δ 0.71 ppm. All spectroscopic data in agreement with that
previously reported.17
