$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM BAIB (24.7 mg, 76.6 µmol) and TEMPO (2.4 mg, 15.3 µmol) were added to a
stirred solution of diol 20 (19.0 mg, 69.5 µmol) in wet CH2Cl2 (3 mL).
The reaction mixture was stirred for 24 h and quenched with saturated
Na2S2O3 (5 mL) and poured into CH2Cl2 (10 mL). The layers were separated
and the aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 × 10 mL). The combined
organic extracts were washed with aqueous NaHCO3 (10 mL) and brine (10
mL), dried with Na2SO4, filtered and evaporated under reduced pressure to
give crude hydroxyaldehyde 25 (17.5 mg, 64.6 µmol, 93%) as an oil which
did not require any further purification. Rf (20% Me2CO-petrol) 0.36; IR
(thin film, cm-1) 3520, 2988, 2924, 2852, 1726, 1694, 1455, 1430, 1385,
1059; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.68 (s, 1H), 4.63 (q, 1H, J = 6.8 Hz),
4.42 (d, 1H, J = 10.4 Hz), 3.93 (d, 1H, J = 10.4 Hz), 3.58 (br s, 1H),
3.10 (s, 3H), 2.21 (q, 1H, J = 7.1 Hz), 1.59 (s, 3H), 1.49 (s, 3H), 1.42
(d, 3H, J = 6.8 Hz) and 1.24 (d, 3H, J = 7.1 Hz); 13C NMR (125 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 199.3 (C), 175.0 (C), 111.3 (C), 88.9 (C), 78.2 (C), 67.7 (CH2),
65.8 (CH), 44.2 (CH), 29.0 (CH3), 25.7 (CH3), 25.5 (CH3), 18.4 (CH3) and
9.4 (CH3); LRMS (ESI, m/z) 362 (M + MeOH + NH4+ + MeCN, 100%); HRMS (FI)
calcd for C13H22NO5 (M + H+) 272.1498; found 272.1493 (∆ 1.7 ppm).
