$DATUM Compound (26): To a solution of well stirred diol 24 (157 mg, 0.5 mmol, 1
eq) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (2.5 mL) was consequently added PhI(OAc)2 (177.10
mg, 0.55 mmol, 1.1 eq) and TEMPO (15.62 mg, 0.1 mmol, 0.2 eq) under
nitrogen atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred for 2 h. The
solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure to afford the crude product
which was passed through a short pad silica gel, the solvent was removed
under reduced pressure to afford aldehyde 25. Without further
characterisation of the aldehyde 25 taken ahead to the next step. Light
yellow colour oil (143.5 mg, 0.46 mmol), 92% crude yield.
