$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Hydroxy aldehyde (+)-56-1: To a solution of diol (+)-56 (13 mg, 0.0165
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (0.8 mL) at 25 °C was added PhI(OAc)2 (3.0 equiv, 16 mg,
0.05 mmol) and TEMPO (1.0 equiv, 2.6 mg, 0.0165 mmol). The reaction
mixture was stirred at 25 °C for 24 h and then quenched with the
successive additons of saturated aqueous solutions of Na2S2O3 (1 mL) and
NaHCO3 (1 mL). The resulting mixture was extracted with Et2O (2 x 5 mL),
dried (MgSO4), and concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude residue
was purified by flash column chromatography (silica, EtOAc/hexanes, 3 -
5%) to afford the corresponding hydroxy aldehyde (+)-56-1 as a white
foam, yield 12 mg, 0.0153 mmol, 92%. Rf = 0.30 (silica, EtOAc:hexanes,
1:9); [α]25D = +118.5 (c = 0.8, CHCl3); IR (film): νmax = 3534brs, 2953m,
2881s, 1703s, 1456w, 1373m, 1249m, 1059s cm-1; 1H NMR (C6D6, 600 MHz): δ
= 10.47 (s, 1 H), 5.55 (s, 1 H), 4.89 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.86 (s, 1
H), 4.83 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H), 4.76 (s, 1 H), 4.67 (d, J = 3.0 Hz, 1 H),
