$DATUM [2S,4S,6S]-2,4,6-Trimethyl-1-nonanal (14). Iodobenzene diacetate (121 mg,
0.380 mmol) was added to a solution of 13 (35.0 mg, 0.19 mmol) and
2,2,6,6-tetramethyl-1-piperidinooxy (10.0 mg, 64 μmol) in anhydrous
CH2Cl2 (1.0 mL). After 0.5 h, the mixture was diluted with CH2Cl2 (5 mL),
washed with saturated Na2S2O3, saturated NaHCO3, and saturated brine, and
then dried (Na2SO4), and the solvents were removed in vacuo. The residue
was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel (pure hexanes) to
afford 14 (32 mg, 92%) as a colorless oil.
[2S,4S,6S]-2,4,6-Trimethyl-1-nonanal, yield (32 mg, 92%) [α ]D +5.6 (c
0.43, CHCl3); IR (film) 1730 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.59 (d, J =
2.6 Hz, 1 H), 2.45 (m, 1 H), 1.09 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 3 H), 0.89 (d, J = 6.5
Hz, 3 H), 0.88 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3 H), 0.85 (d, J = 6.6 Hz, 3 H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 205.5, 45.08, 44.08, 38.89, 38.39, 29.66, 27.86,
20.39, 20.23, 19.94, 14.37 (2 C). Exact mass: m/z 185.1903 (Calcd C12H25O
185.1905).
