$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM TEMPO (1 mg, 0.006 mmol) was added to a solution of the allylic alcohol
(0.045 g, 0.122 mmol), BAIB (0.079 g, 0.244 mmol), and NaHCO3 (0.082 g,
0.976 mmol) at room temperature. The yellow orange solution was stirred
at room temperature overnight. The reaction was then quenched by the
simultaneous addition of aqueous pH 7 buffer and aqueous saturated sodium
thiosulfate. The phases were separated and the aqueous layer was
extracted three times with CH2Cl2. The combined organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to yield a yellow-white
solid which was purified by column chromatography (using a gradient of
100:0 - 97:3, hexanes/EtOAc) to yield aldehyde 10. Colorless oil, yield
0.041 g, 0.112 mmol, 92%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 9.36 (s, 1H),
7.65 - 7.63 (m, 4H), 7.46 - 7.36 (m, 6H), 6.29 (d, J = 9.8 Hz, 1H), 3.66
(dd, J = 9.7, 5,4 Hz, 1H), 3.59 (dd, J = 9.7, 6.7 Hz, 1H), 2.98 - 2.88
(m, 1H), 1.73 (s, 3H), 1.07 (d, J = 6.7 Hz, 3H), 1.04 (s, 9H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 195.6, 157.3, 139.4, 135.8, 135.7, 133.6,
133.6, 129.9, 129.9, 127.9, 67.7, 36.6, 26.9, 19.4, 16.2, 9.6.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM literature preparation, buffered solution used in stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
