$DATUM Aldehyde- 10: To a stirred solution of alcohol 9 (3.1 g, 14.4 mmol) in
dry DCM (20 mL) at 0 °C was added iodobenzenediacetate (5.59 g, 17.3
mmol) followed by TEMPO (225 mg, 1.44 mmol) and allowed the reaction
mixture to stir at ambient temperature for 3h. After this the reaction
mixture was partitioned between saturated aqueous solution of hypo and
DCM, extracted with DCM (3x30 mL). The organic extracts were combined,
washed with brine, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, evaporated under reduced
pressure, purified on silica gel (8% EtOAc/hexanes) to furnish the
aldehyde as liquid 10 (2.78 g, 91%). Rf = 0.6 (20% EtOAc/hexane). [α]25 D
: -10.8 (c = 0.6, CHCl3 ); IR (KBr) 2850, 2720, 1710, 1120 cm-1 1H NMR
(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 9.73 (d, J = 3.1 Hz, 1H), 4.30 (q, J = 6.7 Hz,
1H),4.10 (dd, J = 8.0, 6.3 Hz, 1H), 3.70 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 1H), 2.34 (m,
1H), 1.56-1.38 (m, 12H), 0.94 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H).13C NMR (CDCl3, 100
MHz): δ 203.4, 110.0, 74.9, 67.4, 56.9, 36.0, 34.8, 25.0, 23.8, 23.7,
19.4, 11.6; MS-ESI (m/z) [M+Na]+ : 235.2; HRMS: calculated for C12H20O3
Na [M+Na]+ : 235.1310 found 235.1321.
