$DATUM (S)-2-(tert-butyldiphenylsilyloxy)-4-oxobutyl pivalate (8). To a solution
of 7 (297 mg, 0.694 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (10 mL) was added BAIB (257 mg, 0.798
mmol) and a catalytic amount of TEMPO. The reaction mixture was stirred
at room temperature for 5 hours. Evaporation gave a residue, which was
dissolved in tBuOMe (5 mL) and washed with a solution 10% Na2S2O3 aq. (3
× 5 mL), and satured NaHCO3 aq. (3 × 5 mL). After drying with Na2SO4 and
solvent evaporated under reduced pressure, the residue was purified by
chromatography on silica-gel (5% EtOAc/Hexane) affording compound. Yield:
270 mg (91%); orange oil. Rf = 0.42 (20% EtOAc/Hexane); [α]D19 = -9.8 (c
0.9, CHCl3); IR (NaCl, neat): 2946, 2878, 1735, 1716 cm-1; 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 9.72 (t, 1H, H-1); 7.71 (m, 4H, CHo-Ph); 7.44 (m, 6H,
CHm,p-Ph); 4.43 (m, 1H, H-3); 4.09 (m, 4H, H-4, H-2); 1.20 (s, 9H,
tBu-Piv); 1.08 (s, 9H, tBu-TBDPS); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 200.56
(C═O); 178.15 (C═O, Piv); 135.85 (CHo-Ph); 132.92 (C-Ph); 130.13
(CHm-Ph); 127.79 (CHp-Ph); 67.23 (CH2-2); 67.02 (CH-3); 48.18 (CH2-4);
38.83 (C-tBu-Piv); 27.17 (CH3-tBu-Piv); 26.83 (CH3-tBu-TBDPS); 19.22
(C-tBu-TBDPS); MS (ESI+): m/z (%) = 449.21 ([M + Na] +, 38), 427.23 ([M +
1] +, 57), 365.17 (8), 279.22 (5), 221.09 (6); HRMS (ESI+): m/z calcd for
C25H35O4Si, 427.2299; found, 427.2305.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (+)-muricatacin and a formal synthesis of CMI-977 from
L-malic acid
