$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S,E)-tert-Butyl 2-(3-oxoprop-1-en-1-yl)pyrrolidine-1-carboxylate (16, R
= H): TEMPO (9 mg, 0.058 mmol) was added to a solution of alcohol 38 (R =
H) (0.264 g, 1.16 mmol), BAIB (0.934 g, 2.9 mmol), and NaHCO3 (0.780 g,
9.28 mmol) at room temperature. The yellow-orange solution was stirred at
room temperature overnight. The reaction was then quenched by the
simultaneous addition of aqueous pH 7 buffer and aqueous saturated sodium
thiosulfate. The layers were separated and the aqueous phase was
extracted three times with CH2Cl2. The combined organic phases were dried
over Na2SO4, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to yield a yellow solid
which was purified by silica gel column chromatography using a gradient
elution (hexanes/EtOAc, 100:0 - 70:30 by volume) to yield aldehyde 16 (R
= H). Pale yellow oil, yield 0.236 g, 1.05 mmol, 91%. Rf = 0.16 (80:20
hexanes:EtOAc by volume); [α]D22 -55.0 (c 1.73, CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3, 323.1 K) δ (ppm): 9.58 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 6.73 (apparent d, J =
2.7 Hz, 1H), 6.12 (dd, J = 15.6, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 4.54 (br s, 1H), 3.46
(apparent s, 2H), 2.19 - 2.16 (m, 1H), 1.92 - 1.79 (m, 3H), 1.45 (s, 9H);
13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 323.1 K) δ (ppm): 193.0, 157.2, 154.2, 131.2,
79.9, 57.9, 46.5, 31.7, 28.4, 23.4; HRMS-CI (calc. for C12H19NO3 [M+H]+)
226.1443, found 226.1446.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM buffered solution used in stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereocontrol in Asymmetric SE' Reactions of γ-Substituted
α,β-Unsaturated Aldehydes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
